# v300 — OCCURRENCE BRIEF · RISK DISCLOSURE (audit finding EX-02)
#
# projection_occurrence_brief gains data.risk: the complete finding set from
# risk_findings, so counts.at_risk decomposes to its grounds. The function is
# REPLACED in place, not created — its identity signature is unchanged, and the
# brief remains occurrence_brief v1, so no composed projection's version guard
# is disturbed.
#
# v300_brief_risk() is the deployed marker and the only new database object.
#
release          v300
migration        supabase/v300_occurrence_brief_risk.sql
migration_source repository
min_release      v299

function         v300_brief_risk()

# projection_occurrence_brief is REPLACED by this release, not created, and is
# already required from v292b where it is first created. Its identity signature
# does not change, so it is asserted once rather than twice — the same rule
# v297 applied to occurrence_current_venue. The verifier walks min_release
# transitively and checks the union, so v292b's declaration already covers a
# database at v300's level.
